==Russian==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|ru|э́тотъ||ru-PRO}}

===Etymology===
From {{m|ru|тотъ}}, with the expressive prefix {{af|ru|э-}} (from {{inh|ru|ine-pro|*éy}}), winning over {{m|ru|сей}} in the 19th century. Compare {{cog|sa|एतद्}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ru-IPA|э́тот}}
* {{audio|ru|Ru-этот.ogg}}

===Determiner===
{{etymid|ru|determiner}}
{{head|ru|determiner|head=э́тот|g=m|demonstrative||feminine|э́та|neuter|э́то|plural|э́ти}}

# {{n-g|Mostly proximal [[demonstrative determiner#English|demonstrative determiner]]. Usually translated as "[[this]]"/"[[these]]", but can occasionally be translated as "[[that]]"/"[[those]]" and, in some cases, the English [[definite article#English|definite article]], "[[the]]".}}
#: {{syn|ru|да́нный<q:higher register, partial>|сей<q:dated or poetic>|тот<q:partial><id:determiner>}}
#: {{ux|ru|'''Э́та''' [[моде́ль]] [[сто́ит]] [[пятьсо́т]] [[рубле́й]], [[а]] [[вот]] '''э́та''' [[моде́ль]] [[сто́ит]] [[семьсо́т]].|subst=моде́ль//модэ́ль|'''This''' model costs five hundred roubles, and '''this''' model costs seven hundred.}}
#: {{ux|ru|'''Э́тот''' [[я́ркий]] [[объе́кт]] - [[Вене́ра]], [[а]] [[вот]] '''э́тот''' [[мига́ющий]] [[свет]] - [[самолёт]].|'''That''' bright object is Venus, and '''that''' flashing light is a plane.|footer=(''May be used to indicate something physically or mentally distal to the speaker and translated as "that"/"those".'')}}
#: {{ux|ru|[[я|Я]] [[сде́лал]] '''э́ти''' [[рису́нки]] [[вчера́]].|I made '''these''' drawings yesterday.}}
#: {{ux|ru|[[вы|Вы]] [[должны́]] [[неме́дленно]] [[поки́нуть]] '''э́тот''' [[райо́н]].|You have to leave '''the''' area immediately.|footer=(''May be translated as "the" when "the" is implied to mean "this", essentially taking on some of the role of the English definite article, in this case avoiding ambiguity over which region.'')}}

